      "residue_label": "F147",
      "topology_state": "O",
      "extracellular": true,
      "compartment": "extracellular",
      "tag_type": "HA / 2\u00d7HA / FLAG",
      "tag_length_aa": null,
      "linker": null,
      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface labelling under non-permeabilised conditions confirmed for both rat and human ASIC1a (PMC7870742); FLAG-tagged construct used in surface expression panel (PMC8654947). No explicit proton-current assay reported for the 147-site constructs in the cited clips.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L1 explicitly names the junction as between Phe147 and Lys148 in the extracellular loop of rat and human ASIC1a; Python verification confirms seq[147]='F' and seq[148]='K', both within the extracellular span 63-437 and 85 residues from TM1. L7 independently documents a FLAG tag at the identical junction in a multi-channel surface-expression study. L5 and L6 further characterise the 2\u00d7HA variant at this site. No functional (current) assay result is reported for this specific junction in the ledger clips, so validation is surface_only. rASIC1a-147HA148, hASIC1a-147HA148, hASIC1a-147-2HA-148, and ASIC1a-FLAG (F147|K148) full-length constructs expressed in heterologous cells and neurons; used to selectively label surface-exposed channels under non-permeabilised conditions. Constructs are membrane-anchored.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 32996060,
          "citation": "PMID 32996060",
          "claim": "To selectively label the channels exposed on the cell surface, an HA epitope was genetically inserted into the extracellular loop of rat ASIC1a (rASIC1a) or hASIC1a between residues Phe 147 and Lys 148 (ASIC1a- 147 HA 148 , see Fig. 1 A, upper panel)."
        }
      ],
      "plddt": null,
      "conservation_rank": null,
      "median_conservation": null,
      "validation_level": "surface_only",
      "position_evidence": "validated",
      "source_tier": "paper",
      "entailment_verified": true,
      "quote_probative": true
    },
    {
      "site_id": "ASIC1-internal-298-lit",
      "gene_symbol": "ASIC1",
      "uniprot_acc": "P78348",
      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "det_path": null,
      "site_kind": "internal",
      "insert_after_residue": 298,
      "residue_before": "D",
      "residue_after": "L",
      "residue_label": "D298",
      "topology_state": "O",
      "extracellular": true,
      "compartment": "extracellular",
      "tag_type": "HA / pHluorin",
      "tag_length_aa": null,
      "linker": null,
      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "HA tag at 298-299 does not change proton sensitivity (pH-dependent current) nor subcellular distribution of ASIC1a (PMC13155533); surface labelling under non-permeabilised conditions confirmed (PMC7870742).",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L2 explicitly names the junction as between Asp298 and Leu299 in the extracellular loop of hASIC1a; Python verification confirms seq[298]='D' and seq[299]='L', both within the extracellular span 63-437 and >139 residues from TM2. L8 independently reports that the HA tag at this site leaves proton sensitivity and subcellular distribution unchanged, elevating validation to surface_and_function. L4 further documents a pHluorin fusion at the identical junction, confirming tolerance of a much larger insert (~240 aa GFP). hASIC1a-298HA299 and hASIC1a-298pHluorin299 full-length constructs expressed in heterologous cells; HA insertion used to detect surface pool of ASIC1a; pHluorin insertion created a pH-sensitive fluorescent reporter at the same junction. Both constructs are membrane-anchored full-length channels.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 32996060,
          "citation": "PMID 32996060",
          "claim": "Based on the high-resolution structure, two exposed flexible sites were chosen for epitope insertion, the first between Phe 147 and Lys 148 (upper panel) and the second between Asp 298 and Leu 299 (lower panel)."
        }
      ],
      "plddt": null,
